"fluphenazine-decanoate":{rl:"Depot typical antipsychotic started at 12.5 to 25 mg IM or SC per label, not exceeding 100 mg; EPS, NMS and the hydrochloride versus decanoate concentration mix-up are the key risks.",rh:"Fever with rigidity or confusion, severe dystonia, signs of infection with a low white count, or marked hypotension typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"Long-acting esterified high-potency phenothiazine D2 antagonist labeled for patients needing prolonged parenteral neuroleptic therapy, such as chronic schizophrenia.",mp:"High-potency typicals carry the highest EPS risk; the label conversion example is about 12.5 mg every 3 weeks for 10 mg oral fluphenazine daily."},
"dextromethorphan-quinidine":{rl:"One capsule (20 mg/10 mg) daily for 7 days, then every 12 hours per label for pseudobulbar affect; QT prolongation, thrombocytopenia and serotonergic interactions are the key risks.",rh:"Syncope, palpitations, QT prolongation on ECG, bruising or bleeding, jaundice, or signs of serotonin syndrome typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"Fixed-dose NMDA antagonist and sigma-1 agonist dextromethorphan with low-dose quinidine as a CYP2D6 inhibitor, labeled only for pseudobulbar affect.",mp:"Quinidine works as a pharmacokinetic booster by inhibiting CYP2D6, a classic deliberate drug interaction."},
"ciclesonide":{rl:"Inhaled corticosteroid prodrug (Alvesco) dosed 80 to 320 mcg twice daily per label by prior therapy in patients 12 years and older; it is a controller, not a rescue inhaler, and mouth rinsing lowers thrush risk.",rh:"Acute bronchospasm after inhalation, worsening asthma with rising rescue inhaler use, or signs of adrenal insufficiency after a systemic steroid taper typically prompt notifying the provider.",ml:"Ester prodrug inhaled corticosteroid activated to des-ciclesonide by airway esterases, labeled for asthma maintenance (Alvesco) and allergic rhinitis (Omnaris, Zetonna).",mp:"Activation in the lung and high protein binding limit systemic and oropharyngeal steroid effects compared with some other inhaled corticosteroids."},
"flunisolide":{rl:"Intranasal corticosteroid started at 2 sprays (50 mcg) in each nostril twice daily per label, up to 8 sprays in each nostril per day; epistaxis and nasal irritation are common.",rh:"Recurrent nosebleeds, nasal ulceration or septal symptoms, or signs of nasal infection typically prompt notifying the provider.",ml:"Fluorinated intranasal glucocorticoid labeled for seasonal and perennial rhinitis in adults and children 6 years and older.",mp:"Intranasal corticosteroids are the most effective single drug class for allergic rhinitis, with benefit building over days."},
"arformoterol":{rl:"Nebulized LABA given 15 mcg twice daily per label, with a 30 mcg daily maximum; it is a maintenance drug, not a rescue nebulizer.",rh:"New tachyarrhythmia, chest pain, paradoxical bronchospasm, or significant hypokalemia typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"(R,R)-enantiomer of formoterol, a nebulized long-acting beta-2 agonist labeled for long-term maintenance of COPD bronchoconstriction.",mp:"LABA monotherapy in asthma is linked to asthma-related death, so LABAs in asthma are paired with inhaled corticosteroids."},
"olodaterol":{rl:"Once-daily LABA soft mist inhaler, 2 inhalations once daily per label for COPD; it is a maintenance drug, not a rescue inhaler.",rh:"New tachyarrhythmia, chest pain, paradoxical bronchospasm, or significant hypokalemia typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"Once-daily selective long-acting beta-2 agonist (Striverdi Respimat) labeled for COPD maintenance; also combined with tiotropium as Stiolto Respimat.",mp:"Once-daily ultra-long-acting beta agonists include olodaterol, indacaterol and vilanterol; none are rescue drugs."},
"aclidinium":{rl:"Inhaled LAMA given 400 mcg twice daily per label for COPD; narrow-angle glaucoma, urinary retention and milk protein allergy are the key cautions.",rh:"Eye pain, blurred vision or halos, difficulty urinating, paradoxical bronchospasm or hypersensitivity typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"Twice-daily quaternary ammonium muscarinic antagonist (Tudorza Pressair) labeled for COPD maintenance; also combined with formoterol as Duaklir Pressair.",mp:"Rapid plasma hydrolysis to inactive metabolites limits systemic anticholinergic effects; M3 blockade drives bronchodilation."},
"revefenacin":{rl:"Nebulized LAMA given 175 mcg once daily per label for COPD; not recommended in any hepatic impairment, with glaucoma and urinary retention cautions.",rh:"Eye pain, blurred vision, difficulty urinating, paradoxical bronchospasm, or hypersensitivity typically prompt holding and notifying the provider.",ml:"Once-daily nebulized long-acting muscarinic antagonist (Yupelri) labeled for COPD maintenance.",mp:"First once-daily nebulized LAMA; OATP1B inhibitors raise exposure to its active metabolite."}
