"glycopyrronium-topical":{rl:"Topical anticholinergic cloth (Qbrexza 2.4%) wiped once across each underarm no more than once every 24 hours per label, for patients 9 years and older.",rh:"New urinary retention, blurred vision or heat-related symptoms typically prompt stopping the product and notifying the provider.",ml:"Quaternary ammonium muscarinic antagonist labeled for primary axillary hyperhidrosis in adults and children 9 years and older.",mp:"Eccrine sweat glands receive sympathetic cholinergic (M3) input; eye contact after application causes mydriasis that can mimic a blown pupil."}
